From: Donald Hoskins <grommish@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: rawnand: mt7621: poll the status register for ready

The controller's ready/busy path reports "busy" permanently on the
Ubiquiti EdgeRouter 10X: NFI_STA bit 8 is already set immediately after
mt7621_nfc_hw_init(), before the chip has been touched at all
(STA=0x00001100, MASTER_STA=0x0000, nfi_clk=125MHz). Every WAITRDY
instruction therefore times out with -ETIMEDOUT and detection never gets
as far as READID, so the chip is never found even though U-Boot reads it
without trouble.

Use nand_soft_waitrdy(), which polls the chip's own status register and
needs no R/B# signal at all. Boards where the hardware path does work are
unaffected in behaviour; they just poll over the bus instead.

Signed-off-by: Donald Hoskins <grommish@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mt7621_nand.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mt7621_nand.c
@@ -623,16 +623,6 @@
 	}
 }
 
-static int mt7621_nfc_dev_ready(struct mt7621_nfc *nfc,
-				unsigned int timeout_ms)
-{
-	u32 val;
-
-	return readl_poll_timeout_atomic(nfc->nfi_regs + NFI_STA, val,
-					 !(val & STA_BUSY), 10,
-					 timeout_ms * 1000);
-}
-
 static int mt7621_nfc_exec_instr(struct nand_chip *nand,
 				 const struct nand_op_instr *instr)
 {
@@ -655,8 +645,16 @@
 				      instr->ctx.data.len);
 		return 0;
 	case NAND_OP_WAITRDY_INSTR:
-		return mt7621_nfc_dev_ready(nfc,
-					    instr->ctx.waitrdy.timeout_ms);
+		/*
+		 * The hardware ready/busy path reports "busy" permanently on
+		 * this board: NFI_STA bit 8 is already set straight after
+		 * mt7621_nfc_hw_init(), before the chip is touched at all
+		 * (STA=0x00001100, MASTER_STA=0, nfi_clk=125MHz), so every
+		 * WAITRDY times out and detection never gets as far as
+		 * READID. Poll the chip's own status register instead, which
+		 * needs no R/B# signal.
+		 */
+		return nand_soft_waitrdy(nand, instr->ctx.waitrdy.timeout_ms);
 	default:
 		WARN_ONCE(1, "unsupported NAND instruction type: %d\n",
 			  instr->type);
